{
  "name": "beluga-sturgeon",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/fish/sturgeons.py): a beluga sturgeon (hausen), 3.2 m, the biggest fish of the rivers -- massive and thick, the snout SHORTER and broader than a sturgeon's, a HUGE crescent mouth across the whole underside of the head behind four flattened BARBELS; FIVE ROWS OF BONY SCUTES, small and blunt; a small eye; the dorsal fin far back over the anal, broad low pectorals; the SHARK-LIKE (heterocercal) tail with its long upper lobe; grey-blue above, a white belly. Each fin is one membrane sheet. A slow SWIMMER near the bottom (the fish's plumbing).",
